		<defName>CGF1_MWP_Type64_SilencedPistol_</defName>
		<label>Type 64 Silenced Pistol</label>
		<description>Caliber: 7.62x17mm Rimless. 9-round detachable mag. Semi-Automatic.
		
The Type 64 Silenced Pistol is a unique integrally suppressed weapon designed by the PLA in the 1960s, for use in clandestine operations. The integral suppressor coupled with the low velocity 7.62x17mm round makes for a significantly quieter weapon than one could get with a traditional screwed-on suppressor, but the Type 64's stealthiness extends further - using a button mounted on the slide, the weapon's blowback mechanism can be blocked, turning it into a manually-operated weapon and eliminating even the sound of the weapon's blowback. The Type 64 performed well in its role, but was supplemented by the improved Type 67 a few years later due to the Type 64's significant weight.</description>
